From e65aef5b296fbed4a2d49f75f2a3a0a3d5204d20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chan <chan@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:00:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): treat typed image placeholders as text and replay
 custom tools

The tokenizer rejected the image placeholder when it appeared in ordinary message text, even though the DeepSeek API treats a typed special-token spelling as plain text. Protect every added-token spelling in request text, including the image placeholder, before rendering; image content parts add the real placeholder afterwards and remain the only source of the image special token.

The Responses API schema already accepts custom_tool_call and custom_tool_call_output items, but the conversion to chat history raised Unsupported input item type. Replay a custom call through the assistant tool-call channel, preserving its free-form input, and map its output to the matching tool message.

Tests cover text and image-part tokenization and custom call/output history replay.
